# DAQ frontend build-time environment. Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# Vite bakes VITE_* values into the built bundle at BUILD time, so set these when
# you run `npm run build` for the server -- a runtime .env on the box does NOT
# change an already-built bundle.

# ── Control-mode password ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gate for enabling engine-control actions in the UI (lib/control-mode.tsx).
#
#   Local dev (`vite dev`):  leave unset -- the UI falls back to 'diablo'.
#   Server (`vite build`):   set a real value. A production build with this unset
#                            ships with control DISABLED (fail-closed), not with
#                            the 'diablo' default.
#
# IMPORTANT: this is a CLIENT-SIDE check -- the value is compiled into the JS the
# browser downloads, so it only raises the bar (removes the public 'diablo'
# default). It does NOT stop a determined authenticated user from extracting it
# or commanding the backend directly. Real protection against unauthorized engine
# control must be enforced SERVER-SIDE on the control commands (an allowlist
# keyed on the X-Auth-Email header Caddy injects). TODO: not yet implemented.
VITE_CONTROL_PASSWORD=
